MCNPX_Dec_10_2001

This version includes Prael's fix for a problem reported by
McKinney whereby in high-energy-cutoff problems, antiprotons
could undergo terminal processing in CHG_PL, but emerge from
INTERACT with nonterminal events.  A floating-point exception
found by Egdorf and Roberts is also avoided by initializing
the substep-distance to zero for generic charged particles
emerging from the bank below the energy cutoff (this was a
different bug).  Also, LODDAT is promoted to a character
parameter and moved with KOD and VER to a globally-available
include file, eliminating the need for SETLDD.F.  In RUCOM.H,
two parameters were increased at McKinney's suggestion.  The
test problems were updated to cover the bug fixes, and to
include changed answers where appropriate.
The new load date is "Mon Dec 10 14:40:33 MST 2001".

